WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:11.580
In February 1828 Wöhler wrote to his old teacher Berzelius with a confession he

2
00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:12.780
could not keep to himself.

3
00:00:14.583 --> 00:00:20.483
He had warmed ammonium cyanate, an inorganic salt, and watched it turn into urea a

4
00:00:20.483 --> 00:00:25.183
molecule the body makes to dump nitrogen, identical to the natural product down to

5
00:00:25.183 --> 00:00:26.183
the crystal.

6
00:00:28.417 --> 00:00:33.637
He was twenty-seven and understood at once what he held: the same atoms can form

7
00:00:33.637 --> 00:00:36.617
different structures, and structure changes everything.

8
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:43.560
He never claimed to have conquered the field he opened, calling organic chemistry a

9
00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:45.640
primeval forest he had only entered.
